nINFO  2026-10-18T01:21:20 +0ms service=bus type=message.updated publishing\nINFO  2026-10-18T01:21:20 +0ms service=session session=ses_eb3670783ffeVwX3QDgaVavNfV type=finish part\nINFO  2026-10-18T01:21:20 +0ms service=bus type=storage.write publishing\nINFO  2026-10-18T01:21:20 +0ms service=bus type=message.updated publishing\nINFO  2026-10-18T01:21:20 +2ms service=bus type=storage.write publishing\nINFO  2026-10-18T01:21:20 +0ms service=bus type=message.updated publishing\nINFO  2026-10-18T01:21:20 +0ms service=session session=ses_eb3670783ffeVwX3QDgaVavNfV sessionID=ses_eb3670783ffeVwX3QDgaVavNfV unlocking\nINFO  2026-10-18T01:21:20 +0ms service=bus type=session.idle publishing\nI fixed six bugs in `catalog/` and left the tests unchanged. I couldn't run `python3 -m unittest` because I don't have a shell here, so I haven't confirmed the suite passes. I checked each fix by reading it against the tests, and I expect all 16 tests to pass.\n\n- **`fees.py`**: the late fee added the daily rate instead of multiplying by it. It's now `days_late * DAILY_FEE`, so 4 days late costs 1.00.\n- **`members.py`**: `MAX_BORROWED` was 3, but the tests and the policy comment say 5.\n- **`inventory.py`**: `recent(n)` returned one event too many (`[-n-1:]`). It's now `[-n:]`. I also made it return `[]` when `n <= 0`, since `[-0:]` would otherwise return the whole history.\n- **`factory.py`**: added the missing `Emma` book so the sample data has three titles.\n- **`books.py`**: `parse_book` now turns the year into an `int` instead of leaving it as a string, which also makes `age()` work.\n- **`search.py`**: it imported `normalize` from a module that doesn't exist. It now imports from `catalog.text`.\n\nPlease run `python3 -m unittest` to confirm.INFO  2026-10-18T01:21:20 +1ms service=app name=lsp shutdown\nINFO  2026-10-18T01:21:20 +0ms service=app name=session shutdown\nINFO  2026-10-18T01:21:20 +0ms service=app name=mcp shutdown\n", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "params_stripped": [], "param